From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:53:13 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: mpeg4: check the picture data offset without slice
 parameters

Without slice parameters, the first and only segment starts at the
data_bit_offset of the VOP or H.263 picture control. Unlike the offsets
of the slice parameters, it was not checked against the bitstream: an
offset past the end of the OUTPUT buffer was programmed into the bit
reader, and the length of the data to read underflowed.

H.263, Sorenson Spark, and MPEG-4 with resync markers disabled take
this path. Reject an offset that is not inside the payload.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_mpeg4.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_mpeg4.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_mpeg4.c
index a4f156c93..0bdd71a36 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_mpeg4.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_mpeg4.c
@@ -500,6 +500,9 @@ static int cedrus_mpeg4_segments(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx,
 	unsigned int i;
 
 	if (!n) {
+		if (first_bit_offset / 8 >= payload)
+			return -EINVAL;
+
 		mpeg4->segments[0] = (struct cedrus_mpeg4_segment) {
 			.bit_offset = first_bit_offset,
 			.num_macroblocks = total_mb,
-- 
